# Owner conversation

Every reply follows the response contract in @CLAUDE.md. That file is the
single source of truth for how conversations in this repository are written;
this rule exists so Cursor loads it the way Claude Code does.

In short: the owner is not a programmer. Every substantive reply carries, in
order, **Goal** (what we are trying to achieve, restated every time), **What I
did** (exact and technical, jargon glossed inline), **In plain terms** (the
same story with no jargon), **What I recommend** (always a pick, never a bare
menu), and **Next steps** (looking forward; any decision needed asked as one
plain question on the last line). Say what you are about to do before a long
piece of work. Say a failure plainly first. Short questions get short answers
that still end with a recommendation and a next step.
